From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] wmediumd: enlarge hwsim netlink receive buffer

A tri-band EasyMesh lab with 24 hwsim radios produces a continuous stream of
beacons and data frames.  The libnl default receive buffer overflows under
that load, and the kernel drops HWSIM_CMD_FRAME messages before wmediumd can
process them.  This presents as unexplained packet loss even with a zero PER.

Request a 4 MiB netlink receive buffer.  This matches the usual
net.core.rmem_max setting while retaining a warning-and-continue fallback for
hosts with a lower limit.

---
 wmediumd/wmediumd.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wmediumd/wmediumd.c b/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
--- a/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
+++ b/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
@@ -1450,6 +1450,7 @@ static void sock_event_cb(struct usfstl_loop_entry *entry)
  */
 static int init_netlink(struct wmediumd *ctx)
 {
+	static const int netlink_buffer_size = 4 * 1024 * 1024;
 	struct nl_sock *sock;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -1473,6 +1474,18 @@ static int init_netlink(struct wmediumd *ctx)
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		w_logf(ctx, LOG_ERR, "Error connecting netlink socket ret=%d\n", ret);
 		return -1;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A multi-radio hwsim topology produces a continuous stream of beacon
+	 * and data frames.  libnl's small default receive buffer can overflow
+	 * before the event loop drains it, which makes mac80211_hwsim lose TX
+	 * requests before wmediumd can simulate them.  Request the largest
+	 * receive buffer allowed by the usual net.core.rmem_max setting.
+	 */
+	ret = nl_socket_set_buffer_size(sock, netlink_buffer_size, 0);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		w_logf(ctx, LOG_WARNING,
+			"Unable to enlarge netlink receive buffer ret=%d\n", ret);
 
 	ctx->family_id = genl_ctrl_resolve(sock, "MAC80211_HWSIM");
-- 
